      "thinking": "At 22:13:00Z, p50 jumps sharply from ~26ms to 179ms and holds around 190ms through 22:18, while p95/p99 stay flat near 200ms \u2014 the whole latency distribution has essentially collapsed together, with p50 catching up to p95/p99. Meanwhile error rate stays low and request volume and CPU usage remain stable, so this looks like a uniform slowdown rather than a resource or traffic-driven issue.\n\nWhat jumps out is cache_hit_ratio: it plummets from ~0.9 to 0.475 then straight to 0.0, staying at zero from onset onward. That points to a cache dependency failure \u2014 once cache stops serving hits, every request falls through to the backend/database, explaining why p50, p95, and p99 converge to similar values.\n\nI should check whether the cache is an internal or external dependency, and look at deploys/changes around 22:13 to rule out a deploy-triggered cause versus a genuine dependency outage \u2014 pulling logs, change history, and dependency info next.\n\n",
